      \field{abstract}{We show that two known conditions which arose naturally in commutator theory and in the theory of internal crossed modules coincide: \emph{every star-multiplicative graph is multiplicative} if and only if \emph{every two effective equivalence relations commute as soon as their normalisations do}. This answers a question asked by George Janelidze.}
